# Garruk, Veiled Butcher's -2 on turn 3: each player sacrifices a creature of their choice. Bot1 has only an Ornithopter (no
# choice) and sacrifices it, so "if you sacrificed a creature this way" holds and Bot1 gets a 4/4 green Beast with trample.
# Bot2, with an Elvish Mystic and an Ornithopter, chooses the Mystic; it would die, but it is an opponent's creature, so it is
# exiled instead (Bot1's own Ornithopter goes to the graveyard: the control). Loyalty 5 - 2 = 3.
# On turn 5 the -2 again: Bot1's only creature is now the Beast token, which it sacrifices (a token that ceases to exist was
# still sacrificed) and so a new Beast is created; Bot2's last creature, the Ornithopter, is exiled. Loyalty 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
